$$
d_A = \sqrt{R(R - 2r)}
$$

So,

$$
d_A = \sqrt{13 \cdot 1} = \sqrt{13}
$$

Now, the condition is that $ IA \perp OI $, which implies that the triangle is **right-angled at $ A $**, because the line from $ A $ to $ I $ is perpendicular to the line from $ O $ to $ I $.

